body:
Please see the following thread:

https://community.spark.io/t/time-zone-not-working/6572

The code is:

``` cpp
void setup() {
    Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop() {
    Time.zone(-1);
    unsigned char const DEC_BASE = static_cast<unsigned char>(DEC);
    Serial.println( "tn: " + String(Time.hour(),DEC_BASE) );
    Time.zone(5);
    Serial.println( "tn: " + String(Time.hour(),DEC_BASE) );
    Serial.println("");
    delay(2000);
};
```

A work-around is to call Spark.timeSync(); but doing that too often seems to knock the cloud offline briefly.

comments:
[2017-09-15T14:03:03Z | goodchip | comment]
### Small additionals precisions:
The gateway and repeaters have the minimal example sketch provided on the mysensor site in version 2.1.1.

The sensor is flashed with the following test sketch:
```
#define MY_RADIO_NRF24
#define MY_BAUD_RATE 9600
#define MY_DEBUG

#include <MySensors.h>

void setup()
{
  
}

void before()
{

}

void presentation()
{
  
    sendSketchInfo("sensor_test", "v0.1");
    
}

void loop()
{

}
```

The nRF24L01 chips are versions without PA / LNA, and original (not Chinese copies, although I have also tried with).

[2017-09-16T11:13:08Z | henrikekblad | comment]
Exemplary bug report!

The radio has a build CRC check, so getting a corrupt message is very improbable. As you say the most probably cause is that something happens with the message during relaying. A modification of length or overwrite.  

You wouldn't by any chance have access to the relaying nodes log while this happens?

[2017-09-16T11:47:05Z | fallberg | comment]
It could also be interesting to see if signing the messages could affect the behavior. If the repeater modified the message inadvertently, the signature would be corrupt. I suspect this is the case, in which case adding signing would also serve as a validation of the end to end message.

[2017-09-16T12:14:52Z | tekka007 | comment]
The length field is corrupt (ID response msgs have a 1 byte payload) - would be intersting to see the repeater logs and sketch.

8644 TSF:MSG:READ,0-0-255,s=255,c=3,t=4,pt=0,**l=6**,sg=0:197255
8708 TSF:SID:OK,ID=135
