[2017-01-30T21:13:47Z | wborn | comment]
Thanks for having a look at this issue @aounhaider1 . I just made a local build with your fix and now see that the advanced property is part of the REST response. The Paper UI does not seem to use this property to determine if the channels should be hidden when configuring a Thing. 

See also the following screenshot:

![advanced-dynamic-channels](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/12213581/22441565/37345e74-e738-11e6-9e86-ed1b646ad59b.png)

---

---

I'm not sure if Paper UI should also hide advanced channels that are linked when controlling a thing. Currently it does not for these channels:

![advanced-dynamic-channels2](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/12213581/22441569/3ce3a208-e738-11e6-9a8c-fdeadfb2680b.png)

I don't remember ever seeing a "Show more/less" button in the Control view. So this may be a separate  issue.

[2017-01-31T10:05:09Z | aounhaider1 | comment]
I have created https://github.com/eclipse/smarthome/issues/2939 for first issue.
And you are right, show more/less option is not available on Control page at all.

[2017-02-01T00:52:35Z | wborn | comment]
Thanks for having another look at the issue @aounhaider1 . I've made another local build but found that the channels were still not being hidden.

After debugging I think the remaining issue is that the Paper UI code is using `thingConfigService.getChannelTypeById(...)` in `checkAdvance(channels)` and `filterAdvance`  to compare `channel.id` (colorzone0, colorzone1, etc.) against `channelType.UID` (colorzone and temperaturezone).

Here are some AngularJS scope summaries that show what is happening in case of my binding:

```
thing:  { 
    channels: [
    ...
    { 
        linkedItems: [ Lifx_Z_2_Color_Zone0 ]
        uid: lifx:colormzlight:D073D5147687:colorzone0
        id: colorzone0
        channelTypeUID: lifx:colorzone
        itemType: ColorItem
        kind: STATE
        label: Color zone 0
        defaultTags: [  ]
        properties: {  } 
        configuration: {  } 
        showItems: false
        items: null
    } 
    ...
    ]
},


thingType:  { 
    channels: [
        {
            description: Selects the color of the light
            id: color
            label: Color
            tags: [ Lighting ]
            properties:  {  } 
            category: ColorLight
            advanced: false
            typeUID: lifx:color
        },
        ...
    ]
},


channelTypes: [
    ...
    { 
        parameters: [  ]
        parameterGroups: [  ]
        description: Selects the zone color of the light
        label: Color zone
        category: ColorLight
        itemType: Color
        kind: STATE
        tags: [ Lighting ]
        UID: lifx:colorzone
        advanced: true
    },
    ...
]
```

With the following changes I can for instance get the channels on the colormzlight Things to be properly hidden.

controllers.configuration.js
```
function checkAdvance(channels) {
    if (channels) {
        for (var i = 0, len = channels.length; i < len; i++) {
            var channel = channels[i];
            var id = channel.channelTypeUID.split(':', 2)[1];
            var channelType = $scope.getChannelTypeById(id);
            if (channelType && channelType.advanced) {
                return true;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

services.js
```
filterAdvance : function(thingType, channelTypes, channels, advanced) {
    var self = this;
    self.thingType = thingType, self.channelTypes = channelTypes, self.channels = channels;
    return $.grep(channels, function(channel, i) {
        var id = channel.channelTypeUID.split(':', 2)[1];
        var channelType = self.getChannelTypeById(self.thingType, self.channelTypes, id);
        return channelType ? advanced == channelType.advanced : true;
    });
},
```

Would that actually be a good solution? It is a bit unclear to me if  `getChannelTypeById(..)` should use channelId's or channelTypeId's as parameter. Perhaps using a UID might be even better?

[2017-02-01T14:53:26Z | aounhaider1 | comment]
